---

<section class="mac-capabilities" id="features" aria-labelledby="capabilities-title">
  <div class="mac-capabilities__heading">
    <h2 id="capabilities-title">Everything you need, right from the menu bar.</h2>
    <p>
      Start a session, capture an issue, or check in on your day without leaving what you’re working
      on.
    </p>
  </div>
  <div class="mac-capabilities__grid" aria-label="Mac app capabilities">
    <article class="mac-capability mac-capability--focus">
      <div class="mac-capability__preview mac-capability__preview--focus">
        <span>focus session</span><strong>42:18</strong><i></i><b>active</b>
      </div>
      <div class="mac-capability__copy">
        <span>Focus</span>
        <h3>Start a session without switching windows.</h3>
        <p>
          Start, pause, or resume a session from the menu bar, with your current timer always close
          by.
        </p>
      </div>
    </article>
    <article class="mac-capability">
      <div class="mac-capability__preview mac-capability__preview--issue">
        <span>new issue</span><strong>Fix the release notes</strong>
        <small>estimate&nbsp;&nbsp;30m</small>
        <small>today&nbsp;&nbsp;planned</small>
      </div>
      <div class="mac-capability__copy">
        <span>Issues</span>
        <h3>Capture it before you lose the thought.</h3>
        <p>
          Create an issue with an estimate, repository, stream, and Today plan without breaking your
          flow.
        </p>
      </div>
    </article>
    <article class="mac-capability">
      <div class="mac-capability__preview mac-capability__preview--wellbeing">
        <span>today's check-in</span><strong>How are you?</strong><div>
          <i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i>
        </div><small>mood&nbsp;&nbsp;steady</small>
      </div>
      <div class="mac-capability__copy">
        <span>Wellbeing</span>
        <h3>A quick check-in with yourself.</h3>
        <p>
          Log your mood, energy, stress, sleep, and notes, with break reminders when you’ve been at
          it for too long.
        </p>
      </div>
    </article>
    <article class="mac-capability">
      <div class="mac-capability__preview mac-capability__preview--capture">
        <span>add issues</span>
        <code>- Ship install docs #oss/cli ~30m +docs</code>
        <code>- Fix flaky calendar test ~45m @fri</code>
        <code>- Renew team invites ~15m @tomorrow</code>
        <small>3 ready to import</small>
      </div>
      <div class="mac-capability__copy">
        <span>Capture <em>1.1 beta</em></span>
        <h3>Paste a list, get issues.</h3>
        <p>
          Write several <code>- </code> lines with a target, estimate, date and tags. Check the preview,
          then import them all. Lines without a target land in the Inbox.
        </p>
      </div>
    </article>
    <article class="mac-capability">
      <div class="mac-capability__preview mac-capability__preview--carry">
        <span>today</span>
        <strong>Draft release notes</strong>
        <div><b class="is-carried">Carried ×2</b><b class="is-risk">High risk</b></div>
        <small>carry to tomorrow&nbsp;&nbsp;·&nbsp;&nbsp;undo</small>
      </div>
      <div class="mac-capability__copy">
        <span>Carry-over <em>1.1 beta</em></span>
        <h3>Unfinished work moves on, visibly.</h3>
        <p>
          Carry an issue to the next working day in one click. Issues that keep slipping are marked
          stalled, and late ones show as high risk.
        </p>
      </div>
    </article>
    <article class="mac-capability">
      <div class="mac-capability__preview mac-capability__preview--tags">
        <span>focus by tag · this week</span>
        <div><i style="--w: 92%; --c: #82aef4"></i><small>docs&nbsp;&nbsp;4h10m</small></div>
        <div><i style="--w: 64%; --c: #f0a35a"></i><small>tech-debt&nbsp;&nbsp;2h55m</small></div>
        <div><i style="--w: 38%; --c: #c6a8f5"></i><small>client&nbsp;&nbsp;1h40m</small></div>
      </div>
      <div class="mac-capability__copy">
        <span>Tags <em>1.1 beta</em></span>
        <h3>See where the hours went.</h3>
        <p>
          Tag issues and habits, filter by tag, and see focused time per tag in Stats. The filter is
          shared with the TUI.
        </p>
      </div>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>
